title: Vibrations
keyword: VIBRATIONS

Display an animation of the atomic vibrations of a system (normal modes of a molecule or
phonons of a crystal) from the output of a vibrational or phonon calculation. Load the
data, choose a q-point and a mode, and the atoms in the view move along it. Displacement
arrows and a nudged copy of the structure can also be generated.

# Options
- Data: "Load" opens a file dialog for the vibration data (Quantum ESPRESSO matdyn.x
  modes, eig and ph.x dyn files; phonopy ascii, yaml and hdf5; CRYSTAL and Gaussian
  outputs, Gaussian fchk; CASTEP phonon files). The format is detected automatically or
  chosen in the dialog. "Clear" removes the data; the name of the loaded file is shown.
- Q-points (crystals): the table of q-points in the file, in fractional, 1/bohr or 1/Å
  units. Click one to list its frequencies.
- Frequencies: the modes at the selected q-point, in 1/cm or THz. Click one to animate it.
- Suggested periodicity: the number of unit cells that makes the selected q-point
  commensurate; "Set" applies it to the view.
- Animation: "None" stops the motion, "Automatic" animates the displacements with a
  periodic phase, and "Manual/nudge structure" sets the displacement by hand.
- Amplitude and Speed (automatic): size and speed of the atomic displacements.
- Amplitude and Phase (manual): the displacement at a fixed phase along the mode.
  "Create Nudged System" loads a new system with the displaced positions shown in the view.
- Displacement arrows: draw an arrow on every atom along its displacement, with the
  "Length (Å)" of the arrow of the atom that moves most, the shaft "Thickness (Å)", the
  "Head size" relative to the shaft and the "Color".

# Notes
- The animation and the arrows are settings of the view window the Vibrations window is
  attached to.
- The vibration file should correspond to the loaded structure (same atoms, same order).
